course: dictionary
lesson: 9212
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one to use. The word solid is a good example. Ask yourself: is this thing hard and firm, is it not hollow, or is it happening without a break?
explain: «The inner core is a solid ball of iron and nickel.» Here solid means hard all the way through, not hollow. Swap in «hard all the way through» and the sentence still makes sense, so that is the right meaning.
explain: «I read for two solid hours.» Solid here means without a break. Read the sentence with «without a break» instead, and it still fits.
explain: Solid is also one of the three common states of matter, with liquid and gas. «Lava... when it cools it freezes back into solid rock.» Here solid means hard and firm, keeping its shape, like rock.
fact: Solid means hard or firm, and it keeps its own shape, like ice, wood or stone.
fact: «Solid» can mean not hollow, as in «solid gold», which is gold all the way through.
fact: «Solid» can mean without a break, as in «two solid hours».
fact: In science, solid, liquid and gas are the three common states of matter.
fact: In maths, a solid is a 3D shape such as a cube or sphere.
exercise: «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» In this sentence, what are solids? | *Things that are hard or firm and keep their shape | Things that are hollow inside | Things that have no shape at all | Things that are always hot
exercise: «I read for two solid hours.» What does solid mean here? | Very hot | Hard like a rock | Made of gold all the way through | *Without a break
exercise: In maths, what is a solid? | A number with no remainder | A flat shape drawn on paper | *A 3D shape such as a cube or sphere | A straight line with two ends
test: Ice, wood and stone are all examples of which of the three common states of matter? | Fractions | Gases | *Solids | Liquids
test: In «solid gold», what does solid mean? | Cold to touch | Melted into a liquid | Shiny and bright | *Not hollow, the same material all the way through
exam: In health, babies start «solid food» after which food? | Toast | *Milk | Water | Sweets
